<h3 id="Part-(b)-%5B3-pt%5D">Part (b) [3 pt]<a class="anchor-link" href="#Part-(b)-%5B3-pt%5D">¶</a></h3><p>While plotting training and validation loss is valuable, loss values are harder to compare
than accuracy percentages. It would be nice to have a measure of "accuracy" in this problem.</p>
<p>Since we will only be imputing missing categorical values, we will define an accuracy measure.
For each record and for each categorical feature, we determine whether
the model can predict the categorical feature given all the other features of the record.</p>
<p>A function <code>get_accuracy</code> is written for you. It is up to you to figure out how to
use the function. <strong>You don't need to submit anything in this part.</strong>
To earn the marks, correctly plot the training and validation accuracy every few
iterations as part of your training curve.</p>
